From 9fd3ac35795a940370720bd3165b8ba27a54673c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Windows: spool reverse-fetched media to private temporary
 files

On Windows spool files are created in the user's temporary folder with
CREATE_NEW, a random name and a protected DACL for the user and SYSTEM
only; the start-up sweep removes this user's files older than a day.
Spool paths are UTF-8, so removal and size checks go through
spool_file.h (wide-character on Windows, unchanged elsewhere).
